        struct cfl_kvlist *as_kvlist;
    } data;
};
```

## The `referenced` Field

The `referenced` field is a `uint8_t` flag. Per the code comment, it indicates whether `data` is being referenced for `as_string` and `as_bytes`. When set to `CFL_TRUE`, the data is being referenced; when `CFL_FALSE`, the data is owned by the variant. The comment notes that `"Referenced data uses less memory"` while non-referenced variants keep a copy of the original data. It is paired with a second flag, `owned`.

